<article class="env-lemma" id="09GN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09GN">Lemma <span data-tag="09GN">9.9.2</span>.</a> The degree of the minimal polynomial is $[k(\alpha ) : k]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is just a restatement of the argument in Lemma <a href="/tag/09G1" data-tag="09G1">9.6.8</a>: the observation is that if $P$ is the minimal polynomial of $\alpha $, then the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  k[x]/(P) \to k(\alpha ), \quad x \mapsto \alpha  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is an isomorphism as in the aforementioned proof, and we have counted the degree of such an extension (see Example <a href="/tag/09G7" data-tag="09G7">9.7.6</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>